Okay, let me try to figure out this problem. So, we have a function $ f(x) $ defined on all real numbers, and we know two things: $ f(1) = 1 $, and for any real number $ x $, the inequalities $ f(x + 5) \geq f(x) + 5 $ and $ f(x + 1) \leq f(x) + 1 $ hold. Then, we are given another function $ g(x) = f(x) + 1 - x $, and we need to find $ g(2002) $.

Hmm, let me start by understanding the given inequalities and how they might constrain the function $ f(x) $.

